From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Jul 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: skip RECONFIGURE on connected MLO bSTA link and reset reconnect state

Two fixes for MLO backhaul STA stability:

1. When s_updateAllEpMld processes neighbor endpoints that fall into
   the else branch, calling wld_endpoint_sync_connection unconditionally
   triggers a RECONFIGURE even when the neighbor endpoint is already
   EPCS_CONNECTED. This causes unnecessary disruption on a connected
   MLO backhaul STA link.

   Guard the sync_connection call so it is skipped when the neighbor
   endpoint is already in EPCS_CONNECTED state.

2. On a successful station connect event, reset the endpoint's
   reconnect_count and stop its reconnect timer before the endpoint
   may be reassigned to the MLD main link. Without this, a secondary
   link that never gets classified as EPCS_CONNECTED by s_updateAllEpMld
   accumulates reconnect_count across individually-successful
   connect/disconnect cycles until it crosses reconnect_rad_trigger
   and forces a spurious radio toggle that tears the link down.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c          |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
@@ -1427,6 +1427,18 @@ static void s_stationConnectedEvt(void* pRef, char* ifName, swl_macBin_t* bBssi
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pEP, , ME, "NULL");
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(ifName, , ME, "NULL");

+    /*
+     * this event's wpactrl interface itself just reported a successful connection:
+     * clear its own reconnect retry state now, before pEP may get reassigned to
+     * the MLD main link below. Otherwise a secondary link that never gets
+     * classified as EPCS_CONNECTED by s_updateAllEpMld() keeps accumulating
+     * reconnect_count across connect/disconnect cycles that are individually
+     * successful, until it crosses reconnect_rad_trigger and forces a spurious
+     * radio toggle that tears the link down.
+     */
+    pEP->reconnect_count = 0;
+    amxp_timer_stop(pEP->reconnectTimer);
+
     wld_epConnectionInfo_t connInfo;
     memset(&connInfo, 0, sizeof(connInfo));
     connInfo.mldLinkId = NO_LINK_ID;
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
@@ -1663,7 +1663,7 @@ static void s_updateAllEpMld(T_EndPoint* pEP, wld_nl80211_ifaceInfo_t* epIfInfo) {
         } else if(wld_ssid_hasValidMLDRole(pNgSSID) && wld_ssid_hasValidMLDLinkID(pSSID)) {
             // Set ConnectionStatus of all unlinked neighbor endpoints to passive mode
             wld_endpoint_setConnectionStatus(pNgEp, EPCS_PASSIVE, EPE_NONE);
-        } else {
+        } else if(pNgEp->connectionStatus != EPCS_CONNECTED) {
             wld_endpoint_sync_connection(pNgEp, false, EPE_NONE);
         }
     }
